.TH WERKMEISTER-METRICS-REBUILD 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-metrics\-rebuild \- Backfill the metrics event log from record branches, GitHub and transcripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister metrics rebuild\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBWhat it does:\fR
.IP 1. 3
Clones the workspace repo (the origin of \fB<repos_root>/sandbox\-workspace\fR, else \fBoverrides.workspace_repo\fR) into a temporary bare clone, removed when the command ends. The shared checkout is never fetched into or written \" name-check: ignore
.IP 2. 3
On each record branch except the default one, first: copies the lines of its \fBmetrics.jsonl\fR, the events its close\-out pushed (a teammate's too), and caches its \fBusage.json\fR with the branch's git author email in \fB~/.werkmeister/metrics/usage\-branches.jsonl\fR, rewritten each run, for the \fBmetrics\fR report's per\-person rollups
.IP 3. 3
On each record branch: writes \fBstage.done\fR for each stage at the commit that first filled its \fBoutput/\fR, and \fBpr.open\fR / \fBpr.merged\fR at GitHub's \fBcreatedAt\fR / \fBmergedAt\fR for each PR file's \fBurl:\fR (through \fBgh\fR). The ticket comes from the branch's \fBusage.json\fR
.IP 4. 3
Writes \fBask\fR / \fBanswer\fR pairs (AskUserQuestion, ExitPlanMode) from the workspace's Claude Code transcripts still on disk
.IP 5. 3
Writes \fBcoverage\fR rows from the CI \fBcoverage\-summary\fR artifacts of each GitHub repo those PRs are in (through \fBgh\fR), one per package per run: \fBci\-pr\fR for a pull request run, \fBci\-main\fR for a merge\-queue run
.IP 6. 3
Appends each new line to \fB~/.werkmeister/metrics/events\-YYYY\-MM.jsonl\fR, the month of the event's own time
.PP
Re\-running adds nothing: a stage, a PR event, a transcript session, a slice line or a CI run already in the log is skipped. A stage or PR line an earlier rebuild logged without its run's \fBrun_id\fR gets the \fBrun_id\fR in place.
.PP
For a run closed out before its slice was pushed, it cannot rebuild \fBqueue.*\fR, \fBgate.*\fR, \fBrelease\fR or wrap\-up asks: nothing on disk holds them.
.PP
\fBWhen to use:\fR
.IP \(bu 3
Once after upgrading to a version with the metrics event log, to cover earlier work
.IP \(bu 3
Before the \fBmetrics\fR report, for the team view: it brings in every teammate's closed\-out runs
.IP \(bu 3
Before transcripts age out (Claude Code prunes them after about 30 days), to keep their ask/answer times
.PP
The command only appends to the event log; \fBusage\-branches.jsonl\fR is a cache it rewrites, or keeps as is with a warning when reading the branches' \fBusage.json\fR fails. Copy \fB~/.werkmeister/metrics\fR first if you want to undo a run.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
